Section A

1. B) The economy had unemployed or underemployed resources, and moving to the PPF
    involved no opportunity cost.
    
    Opportunity cost is defined as the cost of choosing one thing to do, measured in
    the loss of another good that you would need to give up. For example, the
    opportunity cost of producing 250 tonnes of steel is the wheat that you aren't
    producing. This is because you instead choose to allocate resources that could be
    used for wheat and instead use these resources for steel.

    In this example, the economy is not productively efficient. This means that,
    though all resources may be being used, they are not being used in an efficient
    way. This results in there being no opportunity cost. We know this because a
    policy is implemented; there is no addition of resources to the economy.

    Therefore, there is no opportunity cost when moving from 100 tonnes to 150 tonnes
    of wheat, because the production of steel is not hampered - it increases as well.

2. C) The unemployment rate is positive; the claim about government spending effects
    is positive; but "unacceptable" and the statement about dignity are normative.

    A positive statement is one which is easy to prove wrong because it relies/cites
    a fact or figure which can be looked up and disproved.

    A normative statement is one which is difficult to prove wrong because it relies
    on a feeling or it has an opinion of some sort.

    In this statement, the politician says "unemployment in our country has risen to
    8%", which can be fact-checked and proven wrong. Therefore, it is positive.

    The same goes for "The government must increase public spending to create jobs".
    It is also positive because it can be fact checked based on past instances where
    the government has increased public spending, and the effect this had on jobs.

    The statement about dignity and "unacceptable" is normative because it relies on
    opinion which cannot be easily proven wrong; i.e. it cannot be easily proven
    wrong that work provides dignity and purpose to people's lives. This is a
    subjective matter -> not positive.

3. B) Medium of exchange, because insufficient shells prevent trade from occurring
    efficiently.

    The function of money as a store of value means that money is used to show the
    value of an object when buying or selling.

    The function of money as a medium of exchange means that money is used during
    trade to facilitate exchange with a good e.g. trading $5 for a cup of matcha
    shows how money can facilitate exchange. Though the buyer may not have a good
    specific to the seller, the buyer can use money in order to pay for the drink.

    The function of money as a measure of value means that money is used as a
    placeholder to determine the value of a good.

    The function of money as a method of deferred payment has to do with loans, and
    how money is used to make promises on future payments.

    In this scenario, option B is the most suitable because it relates directly to
    the current problem being faced - that there are no shells to exchange for goods,
    and therefore the shells cannot be used as a medium of exchange for goods and
    services.

